    "stem": "Rehan's school has two taps on the same tank. Tap A alone fills the tank in $4$ days. Tap B alone fills the tank in $12$ days. Both taps run together on that tank.\n\nWhich claim correctly finds how long they take together?",
    "item_type": "mcq",
    "options": {
      "A": "The answer is the one-day rate itself, reported as the filling time.",
      "B": "Add the filling times to get $4 + 12 = 16$ days.",
      "C": "The one-day rates are $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ and $\\dfrac{1}{12}$; together $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ of the tank fills per day, so the tank fills in $3$ days.",
      "D": "Adding the one-day rates also gives the fill time when Tap A runs alone for some days and then Tap B runs alone afterward."
